# Number and timespan literal edge cases, one statement each.
mode: syntax
---- query
1e3s;
1_;
timespan(1.25:00);
timespan(:)
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..4
    LITERAL@0..4
      TIMESPAN@0..4 "1e3s"
  SEMICOLON@4..5 ";"
  WHITESPACE@5..6 "\n"
  PIPELINE@6..8
    LITERAL@6..8
      LONG@6..8 "1_"
  SEMICOLON@8..9 ";"
  WHITESPACE@9..10 "\n"
  PIPELINE@10..27
    LITERAL@10..27
      TIMESPAN@10..27 "timespan(1.25:00)"
  SEMICOLON@27..28 ";"
  WHITESPACE@28..29 "\n"
  PIPELINE@29..40
    LITERAL@29..40
      TIMESPAN@29..40 "timespan(:)"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0003]: a timespan cannot use an exponent
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | 1e3s;
  | ^^^^ exponent used in a timespan
  |
  = help: write the number out in full, or use a larger unit

error[DS0003]: invalid number `1_`
  --> query:2:2
  |
2 | 1_;
  |  ^ `_` must be between two digits
  |
  = help: remove it: `1`

error[DS0003]: invalid timespan `1.25:00`
  --> query:3:12
  |
3 | timespan(1.25:00);
  |            ^^ hours must be 0 to 23
  |
  = help: write `[days.]hours:minutes[:seconds]`, e.g. `timespan(1.02:03:04)`

error[DS0003]: invalid timespan `:`
  --> query:4:10
  |
4 | timespan(:)
  |          ^ expected hours
  |
  = help: write `[days.]hours:minutes[:seconds]`, e.g. `timespan(1.02:03:04)`
